// Trigger Surface Highlight patch - experimental PSM2 terrain-flag visualizer
//
// Recolors loaded map primitives whose runtime terrain/collision flag word
// contains any currently-known SCR surface-test bit:
//   0x10, 0x20, 0x40, 0x80, or 0x00010000.
// This covers the SCR2 low-bit cutscene/dialogue gates and the SCR4
// 0x00010000 dialogue gate. It intentionally ignores unrelated/shared high
// collision bits so the whole map does not become one solid debug wash.
//
// Mechanism:
//   DAT_00355688 = PSM2 primitive count
//   DAT_003556AC = render/A-record array, stride 0x80
//   DAT_003556B0 = terrain/collision record array, stride 0x78
//   terrain record +0x04 = Section D flags word
//
// When the PSM2 loader is about to bake static map packets, this hook walks
// the loaded primitive records. If
//   (terrain_flags & 0x000100F0) != 0
// it repaints render material slot 0 at A-record +0x30 using a bright
// OR-composed palette from the trigger bits, marks that slot as
// solid-color/active by writing 0xFF at +0x38, and clears A.flags bit 0x20
// at +0x70 so collision-only/inactive records can be reconsidered by
// FUN_00211230.
//
// Palette:
//   0x10      -> red channel
//   0x20      -> green channel
//   0x40      -> blue channel
//   0x80      -> yellow overlay
//   0x10000   -> magenta overlay
// Combinations OR together, so multi-bit trigger surfaces produce blended
// colors.
//
// Because this runs at PSM2 load/finalization time, enable the patch before
// entering/reloading the scene you want to inspect.
//
// Hook: replace `jal FUN_00211230` at 0x0022C3A0 in FUN_0022b5a8
// (PSM2 loader finalization). The delay slot at 0x0022C3A4 is NOP.
// This still conflicts with other patches that use the 0x01E00000 cave,
// such as debug_hello.pnach and battle_damage_hud.pnach.

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Hook: replace `jal FUN_00211230` in the PSM2 loader
// Original: 0C08448C (jal 0x00211230)
// ------------------------------------------------------------
patch=1,EE,2022C3A0,extended,0C780000

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// Code cave at 0x01E00000
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// ---- Prologue ----
patch=1,EE,21E00000,extended,27BDFFD0
